{#
    Pushes server-confirmed measurement events into the GTM dataLayer.

    Expects `analytics_events` — a list of {name, payload} from
    App\Service\Analytics\AnalyticsEventFlusher::flushFor().

    The push happens regardless of cookie consent, and that is deliberate:
    dataLayer is a plain JavaScript array in the visitor's own page. Pushing to
    it neither stores anything on the device nor sends anything anywhere, so
    ZEK § 89 odst. 3 — which governs storing on / reading from terminal
    equipment — does not reach it. What consent gates is the GTM *tags* that
    read the dataLayer and transmit, and those are already held by Consent Mode
    v2 (components/_gtm_head.html.twig). Pushing unconditionally is also what
    lets a tag fire correctly for a visitor who accepts later in the session.

    Placed in the body, after the GTM loader in <head>, so `dataLayer` exists.
#}
{% if gtm_container_id and analytics_events is defined and analytics_events|length > 0 %}
    <script>
        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
        {% for event in analytics_events %}
        window.dataLayer.push({{ { 'event': event.name }|merge(event.payload)|json_encode|raw }});
        {% endfor %}
    </script>
{% endif %}
